From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linuxcnc-node maintainers <maintainers@linuxcnc-node.local>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Complete headless backend-only builds on top of --disable-gui

Upstream's --disable-gui and --disable-manpages configure options provide
the headless build itself.  Fill in what a backend-only installation
still needs on top of them:

- Without a GUI, Tcl is optional instead of skipped: when tclConfig.sh is
  found, the Tcl HAL and LinuxCNC bindings (tcl/hal.so, tcl/linuxcnc.so,
  built without Tk and Xinerama) and the Tcl runtime used by haltcl, .tcl
  HAL files and [HAL]TWOPASS are built and installed.  Tk, X11 and the GUI
  runtime checks are still never needed.
- The desktop menu entries, which start GUI programs, are not installed.
- The launcher requires an explicit INI path instead of starting the
  graphical configuration picker, keeps its output on stdout and stderr
  when not attached to a terminal, and never runs wish, while still
  executing an external [DISPLAY] DISPLAY command.
- The Debian build profile pkg.linuxcnc.headless configures with
  --disable-gui, uses a backend-only package manifest and drops the GUI
  build and runtime dependencies; the nodoc profile configures with
  --disable-build-documentation --disable-manpages, skips manpage
  installation and no longer needs asciidoctor.

Builds without these options or profiles are unchanged.
